content.text:
At 1280px and 1440px: `.new-price-sec { padding-left: 5%; padding-right: 5% }`. But local `newPriceSec` base has `padding: 80px 5% 20px`. At 1280px the rule adds `padding-left: 5%; padding-right: 5%` explicitly — this doesn't change anything since base already has 5%.

Wait — but in the local CSS, at 991px the `newPriceSec` has `padding-left: 2%; padding-right: 2%`. At 1280px, Webflow says `padding-left: 5%; padding-right: 5%`. But the 991px rule comes BEFORE the 1280px rule in the media query cascade — the 1280px `min-width` rule overrides the 991px `max-width` rule for screens >= 1280px. But the local CSS doesn't have a 1280px override for `newPriceSec` to reset to 5%! The 991px rule `padding-left: 2%` applies to screens ≤ 991px. At 1280px, `max-width: 991px` doesn't apply, so base 5% is used. ✓

Actually wait — local CSS:
```css
@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {
  .newPriceSec { padding-left: 2%; padding-right: 2%; }
}
```
At 1280px viewport: `max-width: 991px` doesn't apply. Base `padding: 80px 5% 20px` applies. ✓

