Similarly, the left panel's `wayInnerGrid` uses `w-layout-grid` which gives `grid-row-gap: 16px; grid-column-gap: 16px`. The local `wayInnerGrid` CSS has `grid-column-gap: 22px; grid-row-gap: 22px`. The `.way-inner-grid` class overrides these, so the applied gap is 22px. Local has 22px ✓.

Now, the left panel inner grid (`wayInnerGrid`) is a CSS grid with 2 columns, 1 row (2 items). `grid-row-gap: 22px` only matters if there are multiple rows. With 2 items in 2 columns, there's only 1 row — no row gap applies. So the inner grid height = max(item1_height, item2_height_including_margin_top_40px).

OK let me now also look at whether the `wayInnerGrid` in Webflow has a `display: grid` — yes it does (from `w-layout-grid`). Local `wayInnerGrid` has `display: grid` implied by the grid properties. Actually looking at local comparison.module.css:

```css
.wayInnerGrid {
  grid-column-gap: 22px;
  grid-row-gap: 22px;
  grid-template-rows: auto;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  place-items: start;
  margin-top: 30px;
  display: grid;
}
```

Yes, `display: grid` is explicit ✓.

Now let me also check the `wayInnIn2` items — do they have any gap/margin from `w-layout-grid`? In Webflow HTML, they're NOT `w-layout-grid`. They're just divs with `way-inn-in2` class. So no automatic gap from `w-layout-grid`.

The gap fix I added to `wayInnerGridCol2` (`row-gap: 16px`) should add 32px (2 gaps for 3 items) to the right panel height, which should bring it closer to the live site.

But we're still -36px short at 1280. Let me check if the left panel also has a gap issue. The `wayInnerGrid` (left panel inner grid) shows 2 items. With `grid-row-gap: 22px`, the row gap doesn't apply to a single-row grid. But what about column gap? The 2 cards are side by side with `grid-column-gap: 22px`. The second card has `margin-top: 40px` (`.wayInnInDropShadowMarginTop`).

In a CSS grid with `place-items: start`, the second card with 40px margin-top: its cell starts at the same row, but the item inside is offset 40px down. The row height = max(card1_height, margin_top_40 + card2_height). So the row = max(card1, 40 + card2). This makes the left panel tall.

The right panel with 3 items in flex column with 16px row-gap:
Height = item1_height + 16px + item2_height + 16px + item3_height.

The left panel (with inner grid) + 4 text paragraphs + heading.
The right panel (3 chat bubbles) + 4 text paragraphs + heading.

If the right panel is shorter than left, the comparison section (which is a 2-col grid) takes the height of the TALLER column. So if left column is taller in both local and Webflow, the section height = left column height. And if local left is the same as live left, sections should match...

Unless the right column is TALLER in Webflow (due to 16px gap), meaning the section in Webflow is determined by the RIGHT column, while locally it's determined by the LEFT column. Adding 16px row-gap to local's right column makes it match Webflow.

This analysis is getting complex. Let me trust the data: +32px from row-gap on right column should help. Let me now also verify by checking if the comparison left panel `wayInnerGrid` is missing `display: grid` explicitly or gets it from the grid properties:

Local `.wayInnerGrid { display: grid; ... }` ✓.

